 to Lyon by-bicycle. In Lyon, she sees the Rhone.\par 12.\emdash  I go, you go, he goes, we go, you[pl.] go, they go, to go. I act, you act, he acts, we act, you[pl.] act, they act, to act.\par \par NOTES\par }{\b\f210 1.}{\f208  }{\b\f210 R}{\f208 o}{\b\f210 mam}{\f208  and not }{\b\f210 R}{\f208 o}{\b\f210 ma}{\f208 , further down, }{\b\f210 It}{\f208 a}{\b\f210 liam}{\f208  and not }{\b\f210 It}{\f208 a}{\b\f210 lia}{\f208 . For a large number of nouns (masc. and fem.) this addition of the }{\b\f210 m}{\f208  corresponds both to movement towards something and to the form of the direct object. }{\b\f210 V}{\f208 i}{\b\f210 sito It}{\f208 a}{\b\f210 liam}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 I am visiting Italy}{\f208 .\par }{\b\f210 2.}{\f208  }{\b\f210 R}{\f208 e}{\b\f210 ct\u225\'87}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 in a straight line}{\f208 ; \u8230\'c9}{\b\f210 ne}{\f208 , interrogative particle (see L 3, N 3). Note the displacement of the accent: }{\b\f210 rect}{\f208 a}{\b\f210 ne}{\f208 .\par }{\b\f210 3.}{\f208  }{\b\f210 In It}{\f208 a}{\b\f210 liam}{\f208 , further down (P 8), }{\b\f210 in It}{\f208 a}{\b\f210 li\u225\'87}{\f208 . Whether it is the answer to the u}{\b\f210 bi}{\f208 ? question or to the }{\b\f210 quo}{\f208 ? question one puts the preposition }{\b\f210 in}{\f208  before the names of countries or things, but not in front of the names of cities, nor in front of }{\b\f210 d}{\f208 o}{\b\f210 mum}{\f208  or }{\b\f210 d}{\f208 o}{\b\f210 mi}{\f208  (}{\i\f211 home}{\f208 ). We shall return to this point later.\par }{\b\f210 4.}{\f208  }{\b\f210 G}{\f208 e}{\b\f210 nuae}{\f208 , another form of }{\b\f210 G}{\f208 e}{\b\f210 nua}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 Genoa}{\f208 . We already saw }{\b\f210 R}{\f208 o}{\b\f210 mae}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 in Rome}{\f208 . In the same way, }{\b\f210 Mass}{\f208 i}{\b\f210 lia}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 Marseille}{\f208 ; }{\b\f210 Lugd}{\f208 u}{\b\f210 num}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 Lyon}{\f208 ; but }{\b\f210 Mass}{\f208 i}{\b\f210 liae}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 